   "text": "A hash table is a data structure that implements an associative array, allowing for very fast average-case lookups, insertions, and deletions. It achieves this by using a **hash function** to map keys to specific indices (or \"buckets\") in an underlying array.\n\nHowever, because the number of possible keys is often much larger than the size of the array, it is possible for two different keys to produce the same index. This situation is called a **collision**.\n\nA hash table must have a strategy to handle these collisions. The two primary methods for handling collisions are **Separate Chaining** and **Open Addressing**.\n\n---",
